Depends: cybroid-plasma (>= @VERSION@), nmap, zenmap, tshark, wireshark, tcpdump, masscan, gobuster, ffuf, whatweb, wafw00f, sslscan, testssl.sh, sqlmap, hydra, john, hashcat, hashid, crunch, cewl, aircrack-ng, hcxtools, hcxdumptool, reaver, bettercap, python3-impacket, python3-pwntools, smbclient, onesixtyone, sleuthkit, autopsy, foremost, testdisk, gddrescue, libimage-exiftool-perl, steghide, yara, binwalk, edb-debugger, lynis, rkhunter, proxychains4, tor, macchanger, wireguard-tools, openvpn, keepassxc, socat, netcat-openbsd, whois, bind9-dnsutils, distrobox, docker-ce, docker-ce-cli, containerd.io, docker-buildx-plugin, docker-compose-plugin
Description: CybroidOS Security: for analysts and security teams
 The industry's toolset: Kali Linux's own tools, Burp Suite and Metasploit
 among them, in a Kali container ("Kali tools" in Launchpad, made on first
 use with Docker and Distrobox); and from Debian, Nmap with Zenmap,
 Wireshark, tcpdump, masscan; Gobuster, ffuf, WhatWeb, sslscan and
 testssl.sh; sqlmap, Hydra, John the Ripper, hashcat; Aircrack-ng,
 hcxtools, Reaver and Bettercap; Impacket and pwntools; The Sleuth Kit with
 Autopsy, TestDisk, foremost, ExifTool, YARA and binwalk; Lynis and
 rkhunter; Tor, ProxyChains, WireGuard, OpenVPN and KeePassXC.
 .
 The same CybroidOS as every edition (look, updates, Hangar), with these
 tools added. Chosen in the welcome at first sign-in, or later in Settings
 (any number of editions together), and installed from deb.cybroid.com.
